            <ArticleTitle>Growth on an arteriovenous malformation: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>661-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of an intracerebral arteriovenous malformation that grew is presented. On the initial arteriogram only one early filling vein was seen in the region where a large arteriovenous malformation was present eight years later. The patient's headaches were relieved by antihypertensive medications. The authors speculate that distension of the AVM caused the headaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
